      "id": "MLC-01",
      "chapter": "global",
      "anchor": "global-minor-label-count",
      "title": "Realized lists consist of separated algebraic integers",
      "statement": "Pairings of the two frames in the common self-dual lattice and their leading determinants are integral. Distinct algebraic integers have product of squared conjugate-pair distances at least one. A vector of half-unit plane cells contains at most one embedded integer.",
      "hypotheses": "A common unimodular row lattice, the two admissible frames, conjugate-pair representatives of a CM field and 1 ≤ j ≤ r.",
      "correspondence": "The concrete integrality statement applies to the actual geometric terms; product separation then applies to any two values of a minor.",
