      "title": "Uniform weighted count at a fixed defect",
      "statement": "The sum of S^(-3r) over every finite set of distinct realized rank-j lists is bounded by 2^j∏(64 R_l)^(2f). Under the standing scales this is bounded by b^(C_c² m² f r), with C_c = 21+4|C_H| for C_l ≥ 1.",
      "hypotheses": "1 ≤ j ≤ r ≤ m, f ≥ 1, H1 = b^(C_H m), L = log b > 1, log rd_E ≤ L/C_l, rd_E ≥ 1, and C_l ≥ 1, in the concrete diagonal setting.",
      "correspondence": "The displayed per-profile geometric series supplies an alternative proof. The source partitions by nonzero support, applies the cubic one-coordinate lattice sum, and then compares the radii with one global height. The diagonal cut also needs an independent dimension upper bound.",
